I think there's something different to be gained from both play styles.
 The traditional approach is more intense in that the player has a lot
more to lose if his character dies.  By comparison, save scumming
encourages a less conservative play style, which can be exciting in its
own right.  I agree that a constant save-restore cycle takes away from
the experience, but I sometimes like taking risks that permadeath
typically discourages.  I've got c43 Mage on d81 right now in ZAngband,
and the difficulty of even some non-unique encounters keeps things
interesting.  With this particular char I tend to save each time I
return to town, which is pretty infrequently.  I've also got ADOM and
Crawl installed and I don't do save scumming with either of those so I
can choose which play style I'm in the mood for.  You won't ever see an
"I won" post for the ZAngband char, but that doesn't make the
experience any less enjoyable for me.


